/target
/dist
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
/handoff.md
# The CANONICAL tank blend is tracked (LFS, `.gitattributes`): it is the source every committed
# derivative — the glb, the LOD chain, the manifest — is cut from, so the two travel together and
# CI can re-cut them. Everything else blend-shaped is local authoring scratch: Blender's own `.blend1`
# rolling backup and the hand-made `.bak` snapshots an authoring session leaves beside it.
*.blend
!assets/tiger_1/tiger_1.blend
*.blend1
*.bak

# Scratch output of `scripts/encode-tank-ktx2.sh` when it is run by hand with default arguments.
# The BAKED glb is the tracked one (`assets/tiger_1/tiger_1.glb`); there is exactly one tank glb
# in LFS and this line makes a second one impossible to commit by accident.
*.mipped.glb

# Firecrawl research scratch (web search/scrape cache)
.firecrawl/

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache
.wrangler/
__pycache__/

# Renders the LOD chain's rendered-difference gate writes when it is pointed at a kept directory.
scripts/lod/out/
